WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.010
In the Eastern Han, Cai Lun gathered tree bark, hemp, rags, and old fishing nets, hoping to make good paper from them.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:18.220
He reported his improved papermaking method to the court, and the emperor and officials were delighted.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:26.410
The workers soaked the materials soft, pounded them into pulp, and stirred it without pause in great vats.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:35.230
Then they lifted a thin layer from the water with a bamboo screen, and it became sheet after sheet of wet paper.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:42.470
The wet sheets were pasted on racks to dry, and sheet after sheet of white, smooth paper was finished.

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:50.340
From then on, paper became an important writing material, helping people preserve and spread knowledge.

